---
title: FERB 0.25.0 — Low-level request lifecycle (current implementation)
config:
  theme: neutral
  fontFamily: Arial, sans-serif
  themeCSS: 'text { font-family: Arial, sans-serif !important; }'
  themeVariables:
    fontFamily: Arial, sans-serif
    fontSize: 15px
  sequence:
    useMaxWidth: false
    wrap: true
    width: 150
    actorMargin: 35
    messageMargin: 25
    noteMargin: 12
    mirrorActors: true
---
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor U as Owner / chat UI
    participant D as Daemon RPC / timers
    participant S as Supervisor / WorkerRuns
    participant B as Context / stores
    participant M as Decision model<br/>(no action tools)
    participant W as Worker runtime
    participant V as Checker runtime
    participant G as Gateway / questions
    participant X as Capabilities / platforms
    participant R as Recording manager

    Note over U,X: Lanes are responsibilities, not nine processes. Model lanes use configured Codex / Claude adapters.<br/>Worker and checker calls reach Gateway through ferb mcp + authenticated daemon RPC (expanded in HLD).<br/>Solid arrows = calls / events, dashed arrows = results. Numbering is a reading order, not fixed action IDs.

    Note over S,V: Shared interaction.md applies to all task-model roles, including recovery and resource review.<br/>Owner-authorized foreground use carries across retries, later owner direction supersedes it.

    rect rgb(235, 243, 255)
        Note over U,X: 1 — INTAKE, CONTEXT AND PLANNING
        alt Interactive chat (or a normal voice turn)
            U->>D: chat.send(text, conversation), subscribe to progress
            D->>S: send(session, text), task can outlive this connection
            S->>B: Load pending clarification, record message,<br/>retrieve memory, recent chat/tasks and environment
            B-->>S: Bounded context, exact resumable task IDs
        else Scheduled occurrence
            D->>B: Rearm recurrence or finish one-shot timer
            D->>S: run_scheduled(saved request, lateness, failures)<br/>Separate schedule session, unattended if a task starts
        end
        S->>B: Search relevant daily activity and action registry,<br/>assemble time / availability / context facts
        S->>M: supervisor.md + context → SupervisorOutcome JSON
        M-->>S: reply / clarify / task, optional control and memory/timer changes
        S->>S: Validate schema and referenced prior task
        opt Invalid schema or unknown task reference
            S->>M: One repair call with validation problems
            M-->>S: Corrected decision or clarification
        end
        break Planning cannot produce a usable decision
            S-->>D: Failure / clarification, no worker starts
            D-->>U: Explain problem
        end
        opt Interactive stop / retry / continue of a prior task
            S->>B: Resolve exact task within this conversation
            S->>S: Stop old run, wait up to 10 seconds for it to settle
            break Stop-only request or old run still settling
                S-->>D: Stopped / already ended / still settling
                D-->>U: Return without starting a new worker
            end
            S->>S: Carry prior goal, result and owner words into a fresh attempt
        end
        opt Interactive turn contains requested memory / reminder / schedule changes
            S->>B: Apply quote-checked changes, record actual results
            S-->>D: Memory / timer events
            D-->>U: Display saved / scheduled / cancelled result
        end
    end

    alt Decision is reply or clarify
        S->>B: Interactive: save reply and pending clarification if needed
        S-->>D: Reply or question, scheduled clarification → needs_user
        D-->>U: Deliver response / scheduled result
    else Decision contains a task
        rect rgb(234, 246, 239)
            Note over S,X: 2 — TASK AND ATTEMPT SETUP
            S->>B: Persist root + logical worker, task specification,<br/>success conditions and original request context
            S->>S: Register in-memory task tree,<br/>worker scopes = union of installed capabilities
            S-->>D: task.created + plan
            D-->>U: Starting task / progress
        end

        par Task lifecycle (while not explicitly stopped)
            loop Worker attempts, continue only on dispatch retry and not stopped
                S->>B: Refresh relevant context, include previous reports,<br/>artifacts and unknown prior ledger actions
                S->>S: New worker ID and run token, start liveness tracking
                S->>W: worker.md + goal / owner words / conditions / tools<br/>Start selected worker type with structured report schema

                rect rgb(249, 246, 232)
                    Note over W,X: 3 — MODEL-DRIVEN TOOL LOOP (zero or more calls)<br/>A tool error is an observation, the worker decides its next action.
                    loop Worker observes, chooses an installed action, then observes again
                        W->>G: tools.call(name, arguments, run token)
                        G->>G: Authenticate grant via RPC, check stop / task / tool / scopes,<br/>validate input schema
                        alt Invalid call or stopped task
                            G-->>W: Structured error, do not execute the action
                        else owner.ask
                            G->>S: route_question(task, question, options)
                            S->>M: question.md + task context (no tools)
                            M-->>S: Answer from context OR ask owner
                            S-->>G: Decision
                            alt Orchestrator can answer
                                G-->>W: Answer, no owner interruption
                            else Owner needed in an unattended scheduled run
                                G-->>W: Declined: owner absent
                            else Owner needed in interactive run
                                G->>D: Pending question, approval.requested event
                                D-->>U: FERB question with options / free text
                                U->>D: chat.answer / chat.approve
                                D->>G: Resolve pending question
                                G-->>W: Answer OR declined / expired<br/>600-second TTL, owner wait pauses watchdog
                            end
                        else Ordinary capability (including browser.login_code)
                            G->>G: Describe target, record tool span, acquire capability locks
                            opt Action kind is outside REVERSIBLE
                                G->>B: Ledger: intended → executing BEFORE execution
                            end
                            G->>X: cap.run(arguments, task / identity context)
                            opt Target recording requested
                                X->>R: Start task-owned capture callback bound to exact tab or window/PID
                                Note over X,R: Sampling runs asynchronously alongside worker actions, the loop below summarizes it.
                                loop Until stopped or capture fails
                                    R->>X: Independent frame capture, preserve action references
                                    X-->>R: JPEG or target/privacy error (halt, no foreground fallback)
                                end
                                X->>R: recording.stop → encode MP4 + receipt
                                R-->>X: Capture complete or partial, content not automatically verified
                                X->>R: recording.inspect → decode saved frames
                                R-->>X: Contact sheet for model / owner inspection
                            end
                            opt browser.login_code requested by worker
                                X->>X: Validate task-owned ref, OTP metadata,<br/>HTTPS field origin and supported input
                                alt Unsupported / unlabelled split OTP field
                                    X-->>G: Error before asking owner, no code entered
                                else Supported field and interactive run
                                    X->>G: ask_login_code(origin)
                                    G->>D: Hidden-code question (bypasses decision model)
                                    D-->>U: Hidden terminal OTP prompt, voice redirects here
                                    U->>D: Secret code / cancel
                                    D->>G: Code directly to pending secure reply
                                    G-->>X: Secret or no answer, clear pending code
                                    opt A code was supplied
                                        X->>X: Revalidate ref / origin, sealed single-field fill<br/>Raw code never goes to a model or normal tool log
                                    end
                                else Unattended run
                                    G-->>X: No code / owner unavailable
                                end
                            end
                            X-->>G: Result / platform refusal / exception
                            G->>B: Finish span, ledger done / failed, or unknown<br/>on exception / cancellation if ledgered
                            G->>D: Redacted action.observed → bus + daily activity
                            G-->>W: Redacted result + status, image if present<br/>Images reach model, not persisted in tool spans
                        end
                    end
                end

                W-->>S: WorkerOutcome: status, summary, artifacts, evidence<br/>Or mapped runtime / provider / unusable-report failure
                S->>S: Revoke run token, stop liveness tracking,<br/>close runtime handles, merge attempt artifacts / evidence

                rect rgb(244, 238, 252)
                    Note over S,X: 4 — COMPLETION CHECKS (automatic after worker claims done)
                    opt status = done, success conditions present, not stopped
                        S->>B: Mechanical checks: file exists / contains,<br/>read action ledger observations
                        S->>X: Read task tab URLs / account observations as needed
                        S->>S: Direct file / URL checks → true or false,<br/>account / ledger / other or unknown checks → model judgment
                        opt Some conditions require judgment
                            S->>V: verifier.md + complete claim / conditions / evidence<br/>Own run token, same worker type and capability scopes
                            Note over V,X: Checker is read-only by PROMPT, not a restricted tool list.<br/>It may inspect worker-owned tabs through validated handoff.
                            loop Evidence queries and fresh reads / navigation as needed
                                V->>G: task.evidence or app / browser / file tools
                                G->>X: Same validated execution path as worker
                                X-->>G: Recorded observations or fresh result
                                G-->>V: Redacted result
                            end
                            V-->>S: Each condition: true / false / unknown + evidence
                            S->>S: Revoke checker token, clean up runtime handles
                        end
                        S->>S: Any false / unknown condition makes outcome blocked<br/>Checker failure becomes unknown, not success
                    end
                end

                rect rgb(255, 241, 231)
                    Note over S,X: 5 — RESOURCE RELEASE AND RECOVERY
                    opt Outcome still done and not stopped
                        S->>X: _release_resources(worker + checker)
                        X->>R: Stop unfinished task recordings before releasing targets
                        R-->>X: Finalization receipts, partial if not explicitly stopped
                        X->>X: Close ordinary owned tabs, detach borrowed / kept tabs,<br/>stop ordinary shell processes, preserve background=true
                        X-->>S: Cleanup records / errors
                        opt Nonempty cleanup records or errors, not stopped
                            S->>M: Reconcile report + checks + actual final resource state<br/>model.resources (no tools, inline prompt)
                            M-->>S: Revised outcome / answer, may invalidate done
                        end
                    end
                    S->>S: Keep bounded attempt reports in memory<br/>Model / tool diagnostics are already persisted
                    alt Outcome done / cancelled, or task stopped
                        S->>S: Leave attempt loop
                    else Blocked / failed / needs_user after execution or review
                        S->>M: dispatch.md + current report / checks / previous attempts
                        M-->>S: retry(worker type, instructions) / ask / finish
                        alt retry
                            S->>S: Keep artifacts / evidence, next iteration uses selected worker
                        else ask
                            S->>S: Leave loop with needs_user and question<br/>This ends the attempt, it is not a waiting owner.ask call
                        else finish or dispatch error
                            S->>S: Leave loop with failed outcome and concrete reason
                        end
                    end
                end
            end
        and Explicit stop may interrupt ANY active task step
            opt Owner explicitly stops the task
                U->>D: Ctrl-C → task.stop, or global ferb stop
                D->>S: Mark stop, stop wins over success / recovery
                S->>G: Cancel in-flight calls, reject new task calls
                S->>S: Revoke active run tokens, cancel task runtime handles
                Note over S,X: No new recovery after stop. In-flight consequential actions can be unknown.<br/>Cleanup still runs. Closing chat / Ctrl-D is NOT task.stop.
            end
        end

        rect rgb(234, 243, 248)
            Note over U,X: 6 — FINALIZATION AND DELIVERY
            S->>X: Final idempotent release on ALL exits<br/>(done path may already have released everything)
            X->>R: Idempotent stop before remaining target release
            R-->>X: Any remaining recording outcomes
            X-->>S: Remaining cleanup records / errors
            opt New cleanup observations and not stopped
                S->>M: Final resource reconciliation, no further worker loop here
                M-->>S: Final reviewed outcome, or failure if review fails
            end
            S->>S: _final: apply stop / verification / cleanup outcome
            S->>B: Persist final task status, answer, spans and outcome
            S->>S: Remove live task, request and gateway registrations
            S-->>D: outcome event
            D->>B: Save task_result for delivery
            alt Chat still attached
                D-->>U: Final FERB answer
            else Chat detached or scheduled run (not cancelled)
                D-->>U: Notify, expose unseen result on next chat.status
            end
            Note over U,D: Cancelled results are marked shown and do not trigger a finished notification.
        end
    end
    Note over U,X: Independent failure lifecycle: silent worker/checker → watchdog cancellation → attempt failure / recovery.<br/>Explicit owner / process / sleep waits suspend the silence timer. Daemon restart marks active tasks interrupted<br/>and unresolved ledger entries unknown, it does not automatically replay the task.
